WEBVTT

1
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.497
Let me out!

2
00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.624
Open the door!

3
00:00:41.584 --> 00:00:42.585
Open up.

4
00:00:44.837 --> 00:00:45.713
Please!

5
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.466
Please let me out of here!

6
00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:51.510
Dad!

7
00:01:34.345 --> 00:01:35.513
Push!

8
00:01:36.972 --> 00:01:38.265
Find him!

9
00:03:18.991 --> 00:03:21.327
Son. You need to get up.

10
00:03:22.411 --> 00:03:23.245
Son?

11
00:03:28.292 --> 00:03:29.126
Wake up.

12
00:03:30.586 --> 00:03:31.503
It's not time yet.

13
00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:33.797
Not yet.

14
00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.177
Get up. Wake up, son.

15
00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:40.638
Wake up!

16
00:05:43.635 --> 00:05:44.720
Thank you.

17
00:05:45.471 --> 00:05:46.972
Who are you anyway?

18
00:05:55.981 --> 00:05:56.857
Who are you?

19
00:07:04.508 --> 00:07:06.426
I'm a magician that cooks.

20
00:07:44.089 --> 00:07:45.883
A magician doesn't follow rules.

21
00:07:47.926 --> 00:07:49.386
They only follow the laws of nature.

22
00:07:54.391 --> 00:07:56.185
I move according to those laws.

23
00:07:58.437 --> 00:07:59.855
Sometimes I break them…

24
00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:03.734
to create

25
00:08:04.818 --> 00:08:06.403
my own masterpiece.

26
00:08:11.742 --> 00:08:13.285
I stand on a battlefield.

27
00:08:14.745 --> 00:08:17.080
Filled with smoke and flames,

28
00:08:17.873 --> 00:08:19.374
it's a battlefield minus the bullets.

29
00:08:31.303 --> 00:08:34.514
Here, I'm an actor
who stands before an audience.

30
00:08:36.016 --> 00:08:36.975
I'm also a writer

31
00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:41.521
and a producer in charge of every detail.

32
00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:00.832
Cooking isn't just about

33
00:09:01.458 --> 00:09:03.460
the happiness of those who eat.

34
00:09:08.507 --> 00:09:10.175
It smells so good too.

35
00:09:10.259 --> 00:09:11.260
Hey, you're here.

36
00:09:12.261 --> 00:09:15.055
The meat melts in your mouth.

37
00:09:16.098 --> 00:09:20.686
Cooking is about the happiness I get
from doing it for others.

38
00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:25.774
I am

39
00:09:26.441 --> 00:09:27.442
a chef.

40
00:10:01.351 --> 00:10:02.894
FAMIGLIA CHEF CHOI SEUNG-HYO

41
00:10:02.978 --> 00:10:07.691
1ST-GEN ITALIAN STAR CHEF CHOI,
A DECLARATION OF LIES?

42
00:10:07.774 --> 00:10:10.235
1ST-GEN STAR CHEF, A MAN OF PRINCIPLE…

43
00:10:23.999 --> 00:10:25.042
Auntie.

44
00:10:38.055 --> 00:10:38.930
Seung-hyo.

45
00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:41.558
You did well today.

46
00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:44.061
Good job, guys. Go on home.

47
00:10:44.144 --> 00:10:46.063
You can go ahead, Dad.

48
00:10:46.146 --> 00:10:47.856
We'll stay to clean up.

49
00:10:48.857 --> 00:10:50.942
There's not much to clean up.

50
00:11:09.002 --> 00:11:10.337
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

51
00:11:13.507 --> 00:11:14.883
I'm sorry, sir.

52
00:11:23.809 --> 00:11:25.435
I know I shouldn't leave at such a time.

53
00:11:27.979 --> 00:11:29.189
I thought long and hard.

54
00:11:29.773 --> 00:11:30.899
Chef…

55
00:11:36.822 --> 00:11:38.407
Thank you for looking out for me.

56
00:11:39.032 --> 00:11:40.283
I'll forever be in your debt.

57
00:11:43.412 --> 00:11:44.329
I wish you all

58
00:11:44.955 --> 00:11:46.081
the best of health.

59
00:11:49.835 --> 00:11:50.877
Do you have a place to go?

60
00:11:54.297 --> 00:11:56.883
Did you find a new place?

61
00:12:06.101 --> 00:12:07.644
I'm going to PL Hotel's La Fleur.

62
00:12:12.482 --> 00:12:14.192
-What?
-Yes.

63
00:12:15.485 --> 00:12:16.403
PL Hotel.

64
00:12:17.863 --> 00:12:19.531
Pyeongyeon Group's PL Hotel.

65
00:12:24.327 --> 00:12:25.412
I'm aware

66
00:12:26.663 --> 00:12:27.956
that Pyeongyeon Group is evil,

67
00:12:28.832 --> 00:12:30.667
and that Plate In Asia
is riddled with corruption.

68
00:12:31.626 --> 00:12:32.502
But…

69
00:12:36.089 --> 00:12:37.174
I must do this to survive.

70
00:12:39.134 --> 00:12:40.093
Because

71
00:12:41.344 --> 00:12:42.637
we can't beat them.

72
00:12:48.143 --> 00:12:49.102
I apologize.

73
00:12:49.686 --> 00:12:52.147
I thank you all for everything.

74
00:13:33.396 --> 00:13:35.023
Good for him.

75
00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:38.193
I'm envious.

76
00:13:38.276 --> 00:13:39.611
I wish I could go with him.

77
00:13:39.694 --> 00:13:42.822
I just had to end up
interviewing here at Famiglia.

78
00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:45.367
Poor me. What rotten luck.

79
00:13:46.743 --> 00:13:47.702
"If you give me a job,

80
00:13:47.786 --> 00:13:50.830
I'll put my heart and soul
into every purée I make."

81
00:13:56.503 --> 00:13:59.339
That's what you told my dad
in the job interview.

82
00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.846
I blurted that out because
I'd failed so many interviews.

83
00:14:17.107 --> 00:14:18.066
Wait…

84
00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:25.574
FAMIGLIA RESERVATION PORTAL

85
00:14:25.657 --> 00:14:26.950
JOIN THE FAMILY

86
00:14:28.451 --> 00:14:29.786
2 JOB OPENINGS

87
00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:31.955
0 APPLICANTS

88
00:14:37.294 --> 00:14:39.337
SOUS-CHEF WANTED

89
00:14:39.421 --> 00:14:42.382
Plate In Asia was created

90
00:14:42.465 --> 00:14:45.051
following the need
for an official evaluation system

91
00:14:45.135 --> 00:14:47.470
that suited Asian cuisine.

92
00:14:47.554 --> 00:14:52.142
Famiglia's chef Choi Seung-hyo
voiced his strong disdain for it,

93
00:14:52.225 --> 00:14:53.893
causing some turmoil.

94
00:14:53.977 --> 00:14:56.605
Chef Choi claimed
some chefs lobbied Pyeongyeon Group

95
00:14:56.688 --> 00:14:58.356
in order to receive a Plate,

96
00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:02.694
and that the system pushes out chefs
that don't cater to Pyeongyeon's liking.

97
00:15:02.777 --> 00:15:06.781
Chef Choi believes
Plate In Asia is muddying the waters

98
00:15:06.865 --> 00:15:08.408
of the restaurant industry.

99
00:15:08.491 --> 00:15:12.537
What does Pyeongyeon Group
think of these allegations?

100
00:15:12.621 --> 00:15:15.498
It's not something we can just ignore.

101
00:15:16.082 --> 00:15:19.002
A lawsuit seems unavoidable.

102
00:15:19.628 --> 00:15:21.254
ANONYMOUS FORUM

103
00:15:21.338 --> 00:15:22.297
THAT HAPPENED TO MY ACQUAINTANCE

104
00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:25.884
My acquaintance almost died
after eating at Famiglia last week.

105
00:15:25.967 --> 00:15:26.968
Seriously?

106
00:15:27.052 --> 00:15:29.137
That's unbelievable.
What kind of restaurant is that?

107
00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:32.932
If they don't even check such basics,
no wonder they never got a Plate.

108
00:15:33.016 --> 00:15:34.309
He can refuse a Plate if he wants to.

109
00:15:34.392 --> 00:15:36.394
Why is he threatening
other chefs to join him?

110
00:15:36.478 --> 00:15:38.938
Who could say no
if an industry leader like him speaks up?

111
00:15:39.022 --> 00:15:40.065
Did you read last year's article?

112
00:15:40.148 --> 00:15:42.525
"I run my kitchen
with understanding and consideration."

113
00:15:42.609 --> 00:15:45.820
To think the smile in that photo
was all for show…

114
00:15:45.904 --> 00:15:47.864
Someone who recently quit Famiglia
exposed Choi

115
00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:49.866
for cursing at and beating staff.

116
00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:50.784
Isn't that chilling?

117
00:15:50.867 --> 00:15:53.161
How can someone be so two-faced?

118
00:15:53.244 --> 00:15:55.205
There's even talk that Choi Seung-hyo

119
00:15:55.288 --> 00:15:58.416
was a bully in his kitchen
and threatened other chefs too.

120
00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:03.004
I was told Chef Choi was against
Pyeongyeon's Plate In Asia system.

121
00:16:03.088 --> 00:16:05.298
I would even say his interest

122
00:16:05.382 --> 00:16:07.592
in the Plate In Asia
bordered on an obsession.

123
00:16:07.676 --> 00:16:11.513
He poked and prodded Pyeongyeon Group
and still couldn't get his way,

124
00:16:11.596 --> 00:16:14.099
so he decided to criticize
something they came up with.

125
00:16:14.182 --> 00:16:16.476
He urged the younger chefs close to him

126
00:16:16.559 --> 00:16:19.104
to return the Plates they received,

127
00:16:19.187 --> 00:16:22.649
and he yelled at and used violence
on those who refused.

128
00:16:22.732 --> 00:16:25.318
You don't think you can get a Plate,
so you'll refuse it?

129
00:16:25.402 --> 00:16:26.403
Good for you.

130
00:16:26.486 --> 00:16:28.530
A great comment made at the perfect time.

131
00:16:28.613 --> 00:16:30.824
But we people
aren't as foolish as you think.

132
00:16:30.907 --> 00:16:32.575
Famiglia, you disgust me.

133
00:16:32.659 --> 00:16:36.955
I'm humiliated to work
in the same industry as you.

134
00:16:37.038 --> 00:16:39.958
Did we go from school bullies
to kitchen bullies?

135
00:16:40.041 --> 00:16:42.085
He spreads lies and steals ingredients.

136
00:16:42.168 --> 00:16:43.211
He threatens younger chefs,

137
00:16:43.294 --> 00:16:45.880
not to mention
committing verbal and sexual harassment.

138
00:16:45.964 --> 00:16:48.800
Trash like Choi Seung-hyo
doesn't even deserve to go to a landfill.

139
00:16:48.883 --> 00:16:51.720
You should be ashamed!
What would your daughter think?

140
00:16:56.099 --> 00:16:58.393
Exactly which day last week
did you visit our restaurant?

141
00:16:58.476 --> 00:17:00.854
We didn't even buy apples last week.

142
00:17:00.937 --> 00:17:02.230
What apple sauce?

143
00:17:02.897 --> 00:17:04.733
The ladies' restroom was backed up?

144
00:17:04.816 --> 00:17:07.068
If that's true,
why didn't you alert the staff?

145
00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:09.362
And Pyeongyeon Group's Plate?

146
00:17:09.446 --> 00:17:10.530
It's not that we didn't get one.

147
00:17:10.613 --> 00:17:13.491
We got one, but refused to accept it.
Get your facts straight.

148
00:17:13.575 --> 00:17:15.201
There was no cursing or hitting.

149
00:17:15.285 --> 00:17:16.578
None at all!

150
00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:23.293
Who's this? Do they work at Famiglia?

151
00:17:23.376 --> 00:17:24.669
-I guess?
-So darn rude.

152
00:17:24.753 --> 00:17:26.254
They must work there.

153
00:17:26.337 --> 00:17:28.089
-Get lost.
-What is your problem?

154
00:17:28.173 --> 00:17:30.717
Losers never run out of excuses.

155
00:17:33.511 --> 00:17:35.889
Yes. I work at Famiglia.

156
00:17:35.972 --> 00:17:38.224
Don't you people
work for Pyeongyeon Group?

157
00:17:38.808 --> 00:17:43.229
Shouldn't valid criticism be based on
what you saw and experienced?

158
00:17:43.313 --> 00:17:48.777
Do you have any idea how hurtful
your irresponsible words can be to us?

159
00:18:33.154 --> 00:18:34.072
Dad.

160
00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.205
Are you asleep, Dad?

161
00:18:49.671 --> 00:18:51.422
Would you join me for a…

162
00:19:18.032 --> 00:19:19.284
Hello?

163
00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.580
Famiglia's owner and chef Choi Seung-hyo

164
00:19:23.663 --> 00:19:26.165
took his own life early this morning.

165
00:19:26.833 --> 00:19:31.796
He ran Famiglia for 39 years
after it opened in 1987,

166
00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:34.007
making him one of Korea's leading chefs.

167
00:19:34.507 --> 00:19:37.677
He was a long-time critic
of Pyeongyeon Group,

168
00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:40.513
claiming they used Plate In Asia
to threaten the restaurant industry.

169
00:19:40.597 --> 00:19:44.183
He even provided various statements
and materials proving his point.

170
00:19:44.684 --> 00:19:46.644
Many praised his courage,

171
00:19:46.728 --> 00:19:49.397
and the media was favorable toward him.

172
00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:52.483
However, the tables turned overnight.

173
00:19:53.401 --> 00:19:57.864
Someone suggested
everything Choi did was staged

174
00:19:57.947 --> 00:20:04.203
because he knew his restaurant Famiglia
would fail to receive a Plate this year.

175
00:20:04.787 --> 00:20:05.830
I was afraid.

176
00:20:05.914 --> 00:20:08.041
I had no choice but to do as I was told.

177
00:20:08.124 --> 00:20:12.629
Going against him would mean
sabotaging my own career.

178
00:20:13.254 --> 00:20:15.965
What can powerless people like us do?

179
00:20:16.716 --> 00:20:20.803
To us, Chef Choi's word was the law,
and we had to follow.

180
00:20:23.181 --> 00:20:25.391
Things only got worse from there.

181
00:20:25.475 --> 00:20:29.562
People came forward to claim Choi
had verbally or sexually harassed them.

182
00:20:30.188 --> 00:20:34.275
Pyeongyeon Group stated
they would take all possible legal action.

183
00:20:34.776 --> 00:20:37.862
It looked like Choi
was well and truly cornered.

184
00:20:37.946 --> 00:20:40.740
Then early this morning,
he took his own life

185
00:20:40.823 --> 00:20:44.911
at his residence after posting
an ominous message on social media.

186
00:20:46.913 --> 00:20:51.376
People suspect Pyeongyeon Group
put pressure on him, causing his death,

187
00:20:51.459 --> 00:20:53.711
and there is a public outcry.

188
00:20:53.795 --> 00:20:55.880
Future statements and the media's stance

189
00:20:55.964 --> 00:20:59.050
are expected to influence
the police investigation.

190
00:20:59.550 --> 00:21:02.053
This is Jung Ui-gyeong reporting for YTS.

191
00:21:13.564 --> 00:21:14.816
"Silence is golden."

192
00:21:17.568 --> 00:21:18.987
Are you all refusing to speak

193
00:21:20.196 --> 00:21:22.365
because your teacher
told you to keep quiet in class?

194
00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:26.995
Why won't anyone say anything?

195
00:21:28.746 --> 00:21:30.957
A situation arose, we have little time,

196
00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:34.168
a solution is far-fetched,
and all we have is money and manpower.

197
00:21:34.252 --> 00:21:36.045
What is it that we need right now?

198
00:21:37.505 --> 00:21:40.383
An overwhelmingly powerful company
sent a poor chef to his death.

199
00:21:40.466 --> 00:21:42.635
The police are investigating,
and people criticize us online.

200
00:21:42.719 --> 00:21:45.805
They're already disgruntled
that we control too much of everything,

201
00:21:45.888 --> 00:21:48.933
and it's a matter of time
before they boycott us!

202
00:21:49.017 --> 00:21:51.102
Do you want to see Pyeongyeon Group
crash and burn?

203
00:21:52.395 --> 00:21:53.312
Is that it?

204
00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:57.316
Pyeongyeon F&B.

205
00:21:58.067 --> 00:21:59.485
-Pyeongyeon Construction.
-Yes.

206
00:21:59.569 --> 00:22:00.945
-Pyeongyeon Global.
-Yes.

207
00:22:01.029 --> 00:22:02.613
-Pyeongyeon Chemical.
-Yes.

208
00:22:02.697 --> 00:22:03.990
Pyeongyeon Media.

209
00:22:04.073 --> 00:22:05.116
-Yes.
-Yes.

210
00:22:06.951 --> 00:22:08.661
You have three minutes.

211
00:22:10.038 --> 00:22:13.875
I expect each affiliate
to come up with a solution to this crisis.

212
00:22:15.501 --> 00:22:17.462
You have 3 minutes, not 30.

213
00:22:18.004 --> 00:22:21.466
No amount of extra time
will boost your creativity.

214
00:22:30.558 --> 00:22:31.684
Two minutes to go.

215
00:22:33.394 --> 00:22:34.896
It's one or the other.

216
00:22:35.938 --> 00:22:38.232
Either come up with an answer
that satisfies me,

217
00:22:38.316 --> 00:22:41.152
or come up
with an incredibly creative solution.

218
00:22:42.111 --> 00:22:46.449
Whether those at this table
deserve to keep their seats at Pyeongyeon

219
00:22:47.200 --> 00:22:49.285
depends on what you say in two minutes.

220
00:22:59.128 --> 00:23:00.254
Pyeongyeon Construction.

221
00:23:02.006 --> 00:23:03.174
Our solution is

222
00:23:03.257 --> 00:23:06.010
to monitor the police and prosecution
as they investigate

223
00:23:06.094 --> 00:23:07.762
before we take any definitive action.

224
00:23:07.845 --> 00:23:09.931
It's hard to say what will happen

225
00:23:10.014 --> 00:23:12.100
-and just how bad--
-Pyeongyeon Global.

226
00:23:12.683 --> 00:23:16.270
We believe our priority should be
to appease those at Famiglia.

227
00:23:16.938 --> 00:23:19.857
From what I heard,
the late Chef Choi's daughter

228
00:23:19.941 --> 00:23:21.192
works there as a manager.

229
00:23:21.275 --> 00:23:24.654
Wouldn't it help to meet with her
and offer our condolences?

230
00:23:24.737 --> 00:23:28.116
If we were to acquire the restaurant
at a reasonable price,

231
00:23:28.199 --> 00:23:31.494
I believe we can reach
an amicable agreement.

232
00:23:31.577 --> 00:23:32.995
Pyeongyeon F&B agrees with that.

233
00:23:33.079 --> 00:23:37.125
We could show our respect for Choi
by upholding the business and persuade--

234
00:23:37.208 --> 00:23:38.334
"Appeasing, persuading."

235
00:23:38.417 --> 00:23:40.878
I have no time
for such vague expressions.

236
00:23:40.962 --> 00:23:44.090
Give me a plan of simple,
concrete nouns and verbs.

237
00:23:44.173 --> 00:23:46.717
What I want is a solution!

238
00:23:54.559 --> 00:23:55.685
Chairwoman?

239
00:24:00.398 --> 00:24:02.942
May I offer a suggestion?

240
00:24:06.279 --> 00:24:07.488
Speak, Ms. Seon.

241
00:24:08.489 --> 00:24:09.615
How about…

242
00:24:12.577 --> 00:24:14.871
we use this as an opportunity

243
00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:17.748
to abolish Plate In Asia?

244
00:24:22.920 --> 00:24:24.714
Have you lost your mind?

245
00:24:26.757 --> 00:24:28.009
Go on.

246
00:24:35.683 --> 00:24:37.435
Koreans are thrown into

247
00:24:37.518 --> 00:24:40.354
a fiercely competitive world
of evaluation at an early age.

248
00:24:40.438 --> 00:24:42.190
At school, at after-school academies,

249
00:24:42.982 --> 00:24:45.776
and even at home,
they're compared to others.

250
00:24:46.360 --> 00:24:48.196
The evaluation follows the same system.

251
00:24:48.696 --> 00:24:49.614
It's all about grades.

252
00:24:50.281 --> 00:24:53.201
For us, the Plate serves that function.

253
00:24:53.284 --> 00:24:56.829
We're sick of living a life
of constant numerical evaluation.

254
00:24:57.622 --> 00:24:59.999
Even if the evaluation system is fair,

255
00:25:00.082 --> 00:25:02.418
if it takes too long,
people get exhausted.

256
00:25:03.002 --> 00:25:04.545
So I had this idea.

257
00:25:04.629 --> 00:25:08.341
If we can't eliminate competition
from our lives completely,

258
00:25:09.008 --> 00:25:12.053
we should give that competition
a reasonable cause.

259
00:25:12.637 --> 00:25:14.722
A grand cause that will bring out

260
00:25:15.514 --> 00:25:16.724
the essence of that competition.

261
00:25:18.017 --> 00:25:21.520
What if that cause were to be followed
by an exciting celebration?

262
00:25:23.689 --> 00:25:25.107
Put that more simply.

263
00:25:25.191 --> 00:25:27.568
We'll select the best Korean chef.

264
00:25:27.652 --> 00:25:28.653
Not the best chef in Korea,

265
00:25:28.736 --> 00:25:30.905
but the best Korean chef
in the entire world.

266
00:25:30.988 --> 00:25:33.532
We won't grade restaurants
by giving out Plates.

267
00:25:33.616 --> 00:25:36.410
The greatest food critics from all over
and members of the public

268
00:25:36.494 --> 00:25:39.038
will select the chef they think
created the best dish.

269
00:25:42.375 --> 00:25:44.627
We'll discard the grading system
to find the best chef.

270
00:25:44.710 --> 00:25:47.505
That's the kind of competition
I'd like us to host.

271
00:25:48.297 --> 00:25:50.007
The best Korean chef.

272
00:25:51.842 --> 00:25:53.135
The best dish.

273
00:25:53.219 --> 00:25:56.931
We'll drop the mask that is Plate In Asia
to pursue the essence of cooking,

274
00:25:57.014 --> 00:25:59.934
and showcase the present
and future of K-food.

275
00:26:00.017 --> 00:26:01.102
We will show everyone

276
00:26:02.311 --> 00:26:05.273
that this is the path
Pyeongyeon Group is taking.

277
00:26:11.028 --> 00:26:12.780
-What would you call it?
-Pardon?

278
00:26:13.948 --> 00:26:15.032
What will the show be called?

279
00:26:16.993 --> 00:26:20.621
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

280
00:26:23.666 --> 00:26:24.875
Korea's best chef?

281
00:26:30.506 --> 00:26:31.424
Yes.

282
00:26:31.507 --> 00:26:35.553
It's titled
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

283
00:26:40.599 --> 00:26:41.475
What?

284
00:26:42.727 --> 00:26:43.561
You don't like it?

285
00:26:44.937 --> 00:26:46.731
It was pretty well-received internally.

286
00:26:47.857 --> 00:26:48.691
No.

287
00:26:49.567 --> 00:26:50.443
It's not that.

288
00:26:51.777 --> 00:26:54.655
What kind of people will show up
and what will they be like?

289
00:26:56.198 --> 00:26:57.283
I just can't imagine.

290
00:26:57.366 --> 00:26:58.617
It's as the name suggests.

291
00:26:58.701 --> 00:27:00.911
We'll gather all the best Korean chefs.

292
00:27:02.705 --> 00:27:05.916
I can't wait to see
what kind of dishes they'll create.

293
00:27:09.628 --> 00:27:11.922
You said it's airing in two months.
Can you even meet that schedule?

294
00:27:12.548 --> 00:27:15.051
I was already preparing a show
with a similar format.

295
00:27:15.134 --> 00:27:17.178
I just have to make a few adjustments.

296
00:27:18.471 --> 00:27:19.347
Thank goodness.

297
00:27:20.973 --> 00:27:24.226
The toughest part
of organizing an event like this

298
00:27:24.310 --> 00:27:29.148
is recruiting the judges,
especially a distinguished head judge.

299
00:27:33.277 --> 00:27:34.153
Guess who we got.

300
00:27:34.695 --> 00:27:35.571
Who?

301
00:27:39.033 --> 00:27:39.992
Henri Bernier.

302
00:27:43.371 --> 00:27:44.372
Gosh…

303
00:27:46.707 --> 00:27:47.792
Henri Bernier?

304
00:27:49.543 --> 00:27:51.212
You scored big, didn't you?

305
00:27:55.257 --> 00:27:57.009
Why won't you join the competition?

306
00:28:03.224 --> 00:28:04.308
Bae Yeong-su.

307
00:28:05.101 --> 00:28:06.352
Yes, Chef.

308
00:28:13.150 --> 00:28:14.610
Did you check with a food thermometer?

309
00:28:15.361 --> 00:28:16.278
Yes.

310
00:28:17.113 --> 00:28:17.947
Yes, Chef.

311
00:28:18.030 --> 00:28:18.906
Bring one.

312
00:28:30.334 --> 00:28:31.252
What does it say?

313
00:28:36.298 --> 00:28:37.466
What does it say?

314
00:28:38.300 --> 00:28:39.927
It's 67°C, Chef.

315
00:28:40.678 --> 00:28:42.930
I told you repeatedly it should be 50°C,
and it's 67°C?

316
00:28:45.182 --> 00:28:47.351
It's so overcooked,
it's as good as burned.

317
00:28:48.853 --> 00:28:51.105
Shouldn't a sous-chef
be able to tell from the color?

318
00:28:51.939 --> 00:28:54.150
I apologize, Chef. I'm sorry.

319
00:28:57.069 --> 00:28:59.572
I forgot and told him to
arroser
the fish.

320
00:28:59.655 --> 00:29:00.489
I apologize, Chef.

321
00:29:01.949 --> 00:29:04.452
Go cook another piece,
and be sure to check the temperature.

322
00:29:04.535 --> 00:29:05.369
Okay.

323
00:29:05.995 --> 00:29:08.330
No, Chef Oh.

324
00:29:09.665 --> 00:29:10.708
Michael Jang.

325
00:29:11.292 --> 00:29:12.126
Yes, Chef.

326
00:29:12.835 --> 00:29:13.669
Finish this for me.

327
00:29:18.841 --> 00:29:19.758
You do it.

328
00:29:20.926 --> 00:29:21.760
Pardon?

329
00:29:21.844 --> 00:29:23.345
You cook the fish.

330
00:29:23.429 --> 00:29:24.680
Make sure it's 50°C.

331
00:29:31.020 --> 00:29:32.062
Yes, Chef.

332
00:29:38.694 --> 00:29:40.112
-Go and finish up.
-Okay.

333
00:30:01.342 --> 00:30:02.259
Sorry.

334
00:30:03.093 --> 00:30:04.720
What were you saying?

335
00:30:04.803 --> 00:30:05.721
Oh.

336
00:30:07.640 --> 00:30:09.517
You really won't compete

337
00:30:10.267 --> 00:30:12.102
in
The Table: K-Chef 2026
?

338
00:30:13.103 --> 00:30:13.938
Right.

339
00:30:14.021 --> 00:30:16.732
What? You'll compete?

340
00:30:16.815 --> 00:30:18.859
No. I won't.

341
00:30:22.071 --> 00:30:22.905
Why not?

342
00:30:24.490 --> 00:30:26.075
I'm already the best in Korea.

343
00:30:28.035 --> 00:30:30.162
Why would I need to enter a competition?

344
00:30:37.461 --> 00:30:39.547
A MONTH LATER

345
00:30:39.630 --> 00:30:41.173
-Hello.
-Hi.

346
00:30:45.970 --> 00:30:47.137
1,000 WON EACH

347
00:30:48.931 --> 00:30:50.599
Ma'am. Can I taste one?

348
00:30:59.733 --> 00:31:01.235
Korean chickens are bigger than I thought.

349
00:31:19.628 --> 00:31:21.505
Ma'am, when did these come in?

350
00:31:30.097 --> 00:31:32.057
Can I have these three too?

351
00:32:23.150 --> 00:32:24.652
FOR THE DECEASED

352
00:32:56.892 --> 00:32:58.435
I never imagined that photo I took

353
00:32:58.519 --> 00:33:00.896
would become your dad's funeral portrait.

354
00:33:03.482 --> 00:33:04.483
Do you remember?

355
00:33:05.693 --> 00:33:06.694
That day.

356
00:33:07.277 --> 00:33:11.031
Your dad and I drank some
makgeolli
I had brewed

357
00:33:11.115 --> 00:33:12.157
before falling asleep.

358
00:33:12.241 --> 00:33:15.744
You must've smelled the leftover
and wondered what it was,

359
00:33:16.620 --> 00:33:20.416
because you ended up
drinking a few sips and got drunk.

360
00:33:21.375 --> 00:33:23.210
You threw up in the yard

361
00:33:23.293 --> 00:33:25.796
and screamed that you were burning up,

362
00:33:25.879 --> 00:33:27.381
that you were going to die.

363
00:33:28.173 --> 00:33:30.008
The ruckus woke us right up,

364
00:33:30.092 --> 00:33:33.011
and we thought
you'd been bitten by a snake.

365
00:33:33.095 --> 00:33:37.141
We stripped you bare and searched all over
to find the bite marks

366
00:33:37.224 --> 00:33:38.100
when you suddenly said,

367
00:33:38.642 --> 00:33:42.104
"The sky is spinning, mister."

368
00:33:42.604 --> 00:33:46.024
"Mister, the sky keeps spinning."

369
00:33:46.108 --> 00:33:47.067
I remember.

370
00:33:49.111 --> 00:33:51.280
It's been almost 30 years,
and I still remember it.

371
00:33:57.119 --> 00:34:02.291
Following the clouds across the sky

372
00:34:03.083 --> 00:34:07.713
Following the flowing river

373
00:34:08.213 --> 00:34:13.051
I just want to wander

374
00:34:13.135 --> 00:34:15.929
Without a destination

375
00:34:17.181 --> 00:34:21.602
With the wind as my companion…

376
00:34:24.062 --> 00:34:25.063
You remember the song.

377
00:34:25.856 --> 00:34:27.691
It was Dad's favorite.

378
00:34:31.403 --> 00:34:34.114
I've never seen
such a fancy memorial table.

379
00:34:34.698 --> 00:34:35.699
Your dad

380
00:34:37.117 --> 00:34:38.410
would be proud.

381
00:34:44.625 --> 00:34:46.168
You old fool.

382
00:34:46.752 --> 00:34:47.878
Why did you leave so soon?

383
00:34:48.712 --> 00:34:51.465
You never got to taste
your own son's food.

384
00:34:52.549 --> 00:34:53.550
You left too soon.

385
00:34:56.261 --> 00:34:57.095
Han.

386
00:34:59.056 --> 00:35:00.307
Yes, mister?

387
00:35:01.350 --> 00:35:02.476
Two years ago

388
00:35:03.727 --> 00:35:05.521
when you came back here,

389
00:35:07.815 --> 00:35:11.693
you had questions
written all over your face.

390
00:35:13.237 --> 00:35:16.657
Did you find the answers
to your questions?

391
00:35:19.201 --> 00:35:21.370
You said you wanted to find yourself.

392
00:35:23.163 --> 00:35:24.206
Were you able to

393
00:35:25.457 --> 00:35:26.542
quench that yearning?

394
00:35:38.345 --> 00:35:44.810
Old memories appear before my eyes

395
00:35:46.979 --> 00:35:51.525
Oh, how I miss those days

396
00:35:53.610 --> 00:35:54.444
Han.

397
00:35:58.115 --> 00:36:00.409
I miss your dad even more today.

398
00:36:20.637 --> 00:36:23.348
Can you please reconsider my application?

399
00:36:23.432 --> 00:36:26.059
We've had zero sales this past month.

400
00:36:26.560 --> 00:36:30.063
So what if we have a restaurant
when there's no income?

401
00:36:30.147 --> 00:36:33.817
I'm sorry,
but you don't qualify for the program.

402
00:36:35.444 --> 00:36:39.406
You've been registered as a co-owner
with your late father for four years,

403
00:36:39.489 --> 00:36:41.491
so you don't meet the qualifications.

404
00:36:42.075 --> 00:36:45.996
You might have better luck
applying for a small-business loan.

405
00:36:47.247 --> 00:36:48.749
SMALL-BUSINESS LOAN COUNTER

406
00:36:49.958 --> 00:36:51.376
I'm sorry, but you came too late.

407
00:36:52.044 --> 00:36:54.129
Applications for this quarter
closed last week.

408
00:37:00.510 --> 00:37:01.470
Yes, hello.

409
00:37:01.553 --> 00:37:04.014
I'm sorry to bother you again.

410
00:37:04.097 --> 00:37:07.559
I've transferred you two million won,
part of what we owe you.

411
00:37:08.477 --> 00:37:12.606
Could you give me another month
to get you the rest?

412
00:37:13.857 --> 00:37:15.317
Please.

413
00:37:15.400 --> 00:37:19.112
I want to repay you as soon as possible,
but we're not doing too well.

414
00:37:21.281 --> 00:37:24.368
Yes, thank you.
I'll get you the money as soon as I can.

415
00:37:24.451 --> 00:37:25.744
Thank you. Bye.

416
00:38:03.490 --> 00:38:04.700
Oh, hello.

417
00:38:05.993 --> 00:38:07.119
When did you get here?

418
00:38:08.328 --> 00:38:09.204
Ms. Choi.

419
00:38:09.287 --> 00:38:11.999
I managed to persuade Chef Cho Deok-rae.

420
00:38:13.291 --> 00:38:16.878
He's finally agreed to testify
that Pyeongyeon threatened him.

421
00:38:17.462 --> 00:38:18.422
Did he really?

422
00:38:18.505 --> 00:38:19.464
Yes.

423
00:38:19.548 --> 00:38:23.719
We need just one more witness,
and we'll have a fighting chance.

424
00:38:24.553 --> 00:38:26.346
A former employee would be the best bet.

425
00:38:27.431 --> 00:38:28.765
That's great news.

426
00:38:28.849 --> 00:38:30.058
I'm so relieved.

427
00:38:31.018 --> 00:38:32.769
I owe you, sir.

428
00:38:32.853 --> 00:38:34.646
Thank you so much.

429
00:38:36.857 --> 00:38:41.486
It won't be easy to find someone
to testify on our behalf.

430
00:38:41.570 --> 00:38:42.863
But still,

431
00:38:42.946 --> 00:38:46.116
I'll see what I can do.

432
00:38:48.785 --> 00:38:50.746
A former Famiglia employee…

433
00:38:52.330 --> 00:38:54.124
Well… Ms. Choi.

434
00:38:56.251 --> 00:38:57.169
Actually,

435
00:38:57.836 --> 00:39:01.089
I got a call this morning
saying they'd like to meet.

436
00:39:04.134 --> 00:39:05.093
Who called?

437
00:39:09.890 --> 00:39:10.807
Do you mean…

438
00:39:13.518 --> 00:39:14.644
Pyeongyeon?

439
00:39:16.229 --> 00:39:18.607
She has no intention
of dropping the lawsuit,

440
00:39:18.690 --> 00:39:21.151
and won't accept any of our offers?

441
00:39:25.906 --> 00:39:27.282
What is it that she wants then?

442
00:39:28.366 --> 00:39:31.119
She can't be against everything.
There must be something she wants.

443
00:39:39.086 --> 00:39:40.337
Ms. Baek Hyeon-ju?

444
00:39:45.050 --> 00:39:47.385
Well, it seems…

445
00:39:48.428 --> 00:39:51.098
she doesn't really want anything.

446
00:39:51.181 --> 00:39:54.559
She just went on
about her father's honor and…

447
00:39:56.436 --> 00:40:00.232
Accepting our offer would honor
Chef Choi's name and memory.

448
00:40:00.315 --> 00:40:02.442
It'd help the restaurant's
reputation too, right?

449
00:40:03.026 --> 00:40:04.361
It would, but…

450
00:40:06.321 --> 00:40:10.951
I think the brat wants
something more than that.

451
00:40:14.371 --> 00:40:18.458
She said she'd sue Pyeongyeon Group
to reveal the truth.

452
00:40:19.751 --> 00:40:24.506
She kept sprouting unrealistic nonsense,
and it's driving me crazy, Hae-seon.

453
00:40:26.383 --> 00:40:30.554
It looks like things are
about to get messy for us.

454
00:40:31.471 --> 00:40:34.808
Apparently, some chefs came forward
to say we threatened them to lie.

455
00:40:35.767 --> 00:40:40.605
She said something
about getting witness statements.

456
00:40:46.111 --> 00:40:50.115
She insists on going to court
when it could take one year or ten?

457
00:40:51.032 --> 00:40:52.033
Against Pyeongyeon Group?

458
00:40:52.117 --> 00:40:53.535
Yes!

459
00:40:54.077 --> 00:40:55.579
She's crazy, I tell you!

460
00:40:56.079 --> 00:40:58.915
She's a nutcase. A total psycho.

461
00:40:58.999 --> 00:41:00.000
That's right.

462
00:41:01.084 --> 00:41:04.254
I'm a psycho nutcase.

463
00:41:07.382 --> 00:41:08.508
Just so you know,

464
00:41:09.593 --> 00:41:11.428
there's no cure for a psycho.

465
00:41:11.511 --> 00:41:13.305
You little…

466
00:41:30.614 --> 00:41:32.073
She doesn't want money,

467
00:41:32.157 --> 00:41:35.577
and she doesn't want our help
to restore Famiglia's honor either.

468
00:41:35.660 --> 00:41:38.330
Win or lose,
she'll take this fight all the way.

469
00:41:38.997 --> 00:41:43.418
She wants to tell the whole world
that her father died…

470
00:41:45.503 --> 00:41:47.088
because of our manipulation and threats?

471
00:41:52.969 --> 00:41:55.430
The more complicated something is,
the more problems it brings.

472
00:41:57.724 --> 00:42:00.602
Editing recordings,
blackmailing those involved,

473
00:42:00.685 --> 00:42:02.020
inducing false statements,

474
00:42:02.520 --> 00:42:04.981
bribery, and hiring people
to post comments online.

475
00:42:06.066 --> 00:42:10.695
Did you think such old tactics would work
in this day and age?

476
00:42:11.738 --> 00:42:13.156
Baek Chun-ja.

477
00:42:18.912 --> 00:42:20.789
The competition kicks off in a month.

478
00:42:21.498 --> 00:42:24.751
The project is our best shot
at easing the Famiglia crisis.

479
00:42:24.834 --> 00:42:28.463
We're giving up on Plate In Asia
to find the best Korean chef.

480
00:42:29.673 --> 00:42:31.841
That's how prestigious
this competition is.

481
00:42:32.884 --> 00:42:36.429
We can't host that
while Famiglia is suing us, can we?

482
00:42:37.722 --> 00:42:42.352
If people were to think
we drove a respected chef to his death,

483
00:42:42.936 --> 00:42:45.480
would they care to watch our competition?

484
00:42:49.943 --> 00:42:51.027
Come on, Chun-ja.

485
00:42:57.409 --> 00:43:00.912
I'd love to chop up
the neck of that darn viper!

486
00:43:09.629 --> 00:43:13.174
She made me the CEO of a cable TV station
the size of a corner store,

487
00:43:13.758 --> 00:43:15.343
and keeps calling me by my old name.

488
00:43:15.844 --> 00:43:17.721
"Hey, Baek Chun-ja."

489
00:43:17.804 --> 00:43:19.222
Darn it.

490
00:43:19.306 --> 00:43:21.308
I'm not Baek Chun-ja!

491
00:43:22.851 --> 00:43:25.603
You think I did all that for my sake?

492
00:43:25.687 --> 00:43:27.439
I did it for the company.

493
00:43:27.522 --> 00:43:29.899
For Pyeongyeon Group, the darn company.

494
00:43:29.983 --> 00:43:31.151
For Pyeongyeon!

495
00:43:36.489 --> 00:43:37.324
What's wrong?

496
00:43:37.407 --> 00:43:38.616
Are you hurt?

497
00:43:41.411 --> 00:43:42.287
I'm fine.

498
00:43:42.370 --> 00:43:45.165
I can handle this much.
It's no problem.

499
00:43:45.248 --> 00:43:48.001
Yeah, you're fine. It's nothing.

500
00:43:48.626 --> 00:43:49.711
Leave it!

501
00:43:51.755 --> 00:43:52.672
"This much"?

502
00:43:54.257 --> 00:43:55.175
"This much"?

503
00:43:56.301 --> 00:43:57.344
"This much"?

504
00:43:58.011 --> 00:44:00.847
Hey. Are you looking down on me too?

505
00:44:00.930 --> 00:44:02.515
-Sorry?
-Do you?

506
00:44:03.475 --> 00:44:04.601
-Do you?
-No.

507
00:44:04.684 --> 00:44:05.560
Just because

508
00:44:06.519 --> 00:44:09.230
I'm an illegitimate child
who was taken in by the family,

509
00:44:10.023 --> 00:44:12.859
are you looking down on me too?

510
00:44:13.943 --> 00:44:15.403
-Ma'am.
-Do you?

511
00:44:15.487 --> 00:44:17.072
No. That's not it.

512
00:44:17.155 --> 00:44:18.323
I'm sorry.

513
00:44:18.907 --> 00:44:19.866
I apologize.

514
00:44:19.949 --> 00:44:21.910
It wasn't like that, I swear.

515
00:44:23.119 --> 00:44:23.953
Open the email.

516
00:44:26.247 --> 00:44:27.582
What the…

517
00:44:27.665 --> 00:44:30.085
Why is she sending me an email
in the middle of the night?

518
00:44:30.668 --> 00:44:34.297
Still, it's about the head judge,
so I should check it out.

519
00:44:34.381 --> 00:44:35.423
Let's see.

520
00:44:35.507 --> 00:44:36.841
GOURMET COLUMNIST, AUTHOR,
INTERNATIONAL CULINARY COMPETITION JUDGE

521
00:44:36.925 --> 00:44:38.259
I know all this already.

522
00:44:38.343 --> 00:44:39.260
Next page.

523
00:44:43.098 --> 00:44:43.932
Next.

524
00:44:46.643 --> 00:44:47.477
Next.

525
00:44:49.771 --> 00:44:51.689
FAMILY

526
00:44:51.773 --> 00:44:53.817
SEO-YUN HAN BERNIER, TEXTILE DESIGNER
MOVED TO PARIS IN 1963 TO STUDY

527
00:44:55.860 --> 00:44:57.904
His mother is Korean?

528
00:44:57.987 --> 00:44:59.781
That's why he speaks some Korean.

529
00:45:00.615 --> 00:45:01.449
Next.

530
00:45:01.950 --> 00:45:05.412
3 MISTELLA STARS FOR 13 CONSECUTIVE YEARS

531
00:45:06.037 --> 00:45:07.664
Beautiful.

532
00:45:08.289 --> 00:45:09.916
Fantastic.

533
00:45:09.999 --> 00:45:11.501
That's incredible.

534
00:45:13.628 --> 00:45:16.673
No wonder Ms. Seon insisted we get him.

535
00:45:20.135 --> 00:45:22.220
What time does he land tomorrow?

536
00:45:23.888 --> 00:45:26.808
I'm talking about Henri Bernier!

537
00:45:26.891 --> 00:45:28.476
He arrives at…

538
00:45:28.560 --> 00:45:29.686
At?

539
00:45:29.769 --> 00:45:31.813
At 4:15 p.m.

540
00:45:32.355 --> 00:45:34.274
Have the car ready on time.

541
00:45:35.608 --> 00:45:37.235
You'll go to the airport yourself?

542
00:45:37.318 --> 00:45:39.320
Why not? Can't I?

543
00:45:39.404 --> 00:45:42.240
Isn't Ms. Seon going to the airport to…

544
00:45:42.323 --> 00:45:43.491
Hyeong-koo.

545
00:45:44.242 --> 00:45:46.578
-Hyeong-koo.
-Yes?

546
00:45:47.454 --> 00:45:49.456
We're bringing in a distinguished chef

547
00:45:49.539 --> 00:45:54.169
to take part in an important competition
as the head judge.

548
00:45:54.752 --> 00:45:56.838
I can't send a mere team leader
to welcome him.

549
00:45:56.921 --> 00:46:00.216
Is there anything in that skull of yours?

550
00:46:00.300 --> 00:46:01.926
You're right, ma'am.

551
00:46:02.010 --> 00:46:02.844
Smile.

552
00:46:09.726 --> 00:46:12.270
Rather than the circular layout,

553
00:46:12.353 --> 00:46:15.398
I think this would look
much simpler and cleaner.

554
00:46:16.524 --> 00:46:17.484
Look at this plan here.

555
00:46:17.567 --> 00:46:22.614
It would be a fun idea to film them
running through the hallway to the pantry.

556
00:46:22.697 --> 00:46:25.074
Could we widen the hallway just a bit?

557
00:46:25.158 --> 00:46:26.659
I think we can do that.

558
00:46:32.290 --> 00:46:33.166
Chairwoman.

559
00:46:36.711 --> 00:46:39.130
The concept doesn't look too bad.

560
00:46:40.632 --> 00:46:42.675
When the chefs scatter
to cook in their kitchens,

561
00:46:42.759 --> 00:46:46.846
will the monitors placed above
show what's happening in each kitchen?

562
00:46:46.930 --> 00:46:47.889
Yes, that's right.

563
00:46:50.308 --> 00:46:52.227
Is this where the judges will sit?

564
00:46:52.310 --> 00:46:54.395
That's where the main judges will sit.

565
00:46:54.479 --> 00:46:56.356
And Henri Bernier will sit in the center?

566
00:46:57.023 --> 00:46:58.024
Yes.

567
00:46:58.107 --> 00:46:59.692
He's arriving today, right?

568
00:46:59.776 --> 00:47:00.902
Yes.

569
00:47:00.985 --> 00:47:04.239
Ms. Baek will be
heading to the airport in two hours,

570
00:47:04.322 --> 00:47:06.241
and I'll be accompanying her.

571
00:47:07.951 --> 00:47:10.286
She always wants to be
where she'll be noticed.

572
00:47:13.498 --> 00:47:16.000
Is Cha Woo-jin still refusing to compete?

573
00:47:20.880 --> 00:47:24.300
If Exception doesn't compete in a show
to find the best Korean chef,

574
00:47:24.384 --> 00:47:25.510
it wouldn't look right.

575
00:47:26.970 --> 00:47:28.137
I agree.

576
00:47:28.721 --> 00:47:31.099
Standard tactics won't work
on people like him.

577
00:47:31.182 --> 00:47:34.060
Forget about telling him
the goals, meanings, or causes.

578
00:47:34.894 --> 00:47:38.648
Find a way to appeal to his emotions.

579
00:47:39.774 --> 00:47:40.733
Yes, ma'am.

580
00:47:58.251 --> 00:47:59.085
Thank you.

581
00:48:17.186 --> 00:48:19.105
I need your help, Chef.

582
00:48:19.188 --> 00:48:21.149
I just need you to testify to the truth.

583
00:48:21.232 --> 00:48:23.401
Don't do this.
You're making it hard for both of us.

584
00:48:23.484 --> 00:48:24.861
Haven't you done enough?

585
00:48:24.944 --> 00:48:27.447
I'm not asking for anything else.

586
00:48:27.530 --> 00:48:31.117
Can't you do this for my late dad's sake?

587
00:48:31.200 --> 00:48:32.076
Please?

588
00:48:34.078 --> 00:48:37.749
You worked with my dad for eight years.

589
00:48:38.249 --> 00:48:41.586
You know how much he cared about you.

590
00:48:42.503 --> 00:48:46.049
Just testify that there was
no verbal or sexual harassment.

591
00:48:46.132 --> 00:48:49.677
You know better than anyone
that my dad wasn't like that.

592
00:48:53.473 --> 00:48:55.725
Do you think they'll stop once we're gone?

593
00:48:57.226 --> 00:48:58.853
You know they won't.

594
00:48:59.479 --> 00:49:01.022
If you don't do as they say,

595
00:49:01.981 --> 00:49:05.360
Pyeongyeon Group will do to you
what they did to my dad.

596
00:49:08.613 --> 00:49:09.906
I'm sorry, Song-yi.

597
00:49:10.490 --> 00:49:12.241
Wait. Please, Chef.

598
00:49:12.325 --> 00:49:13.451
Will you give up, Song-yi?

599
00:49:18.998 --> 00:49:20.458
Don't try too hard.

600
00:49:23.252 --> 00:49:24.128
Some things in life

601
00:49:25.004 --> 00:49:26.339
follow a certain path.

602
00:49:56.703 --> 00:49:57.662
Are you all right?

603
00:49:59.497 --> 00:50:00.498
Thank you.

604
00:50:27.483 --> 00:50:28.943
Why didn't you pick up?

605
00:50:31.028 --> 00:50:33.406
Sorry. I put my phone on silent.

606
00:50:37.118 --> 00:50:38.536
What is it, Auntie?

607
00:50:39.245 --> 00:50:40.288
Is something wrong?

608
00:50:42.832 --> 00:50:44.709
Mr. Park, the supplier, called.

609
00:50:45.793 --> 00:50:48.212
He can't supply us
any more ingredients on credit.

610
00:50:48.880 --> 00:50:50.673
He's cutting off our supply
starting tonight.

611
00:50:50.757 --> 00:50:51.632
What?

612
00:50:52.759 --> 00:50:54.802
Then how are we supposed to open tonight?

613
00:50:56.804 --> 00:50:58.055
That's not good.

614
00:50:59.432 --> 00:51:01.267
I'll go and talk to the section head.

615
00:51:01.350 --> 00:51:05.646
He quit.
He packed up and left two hours ago.

616
00:51:06.147 --> 00:51:07.899
What? Why?

617
00:51:07.982 --> 00:51:10.485
I don't know. I begged him to stay,

618
00:51:11.360 --> 00:51:12.653
but he said he'd had enough.

619
00:51:13.738 --> 00:51:15.990
He wasn't getting paid,
and we have no ingredients.

620
00:51:16.532 --> 00:51:17.909
How could he stay?

621
00:51:23.539 --> 00:51:25.541
What should we do, Auntie?

622
00:51:25.625 --> 00:51:26.918
Today's dinner…

623
00:51:27.001 --> 00:51:29.504
We have no choice
but to close for the day.

624
00:51:30.421 --> 00:51:32.715
We have no ingredients and no staff.

625
00:51:33.716 --> 00:51:35.468
Let's be honest.
We don't even have customers.

626
00:51:39.347 --> 00:51:40.181
Song-yi.

627
00:51:40.890 --> 00:51:42.058
How about

628
00:51:42.767 --> 00:51:45.812
we close the restaurant for a while?

629
00:51:46.437 --> 00:51:48.815
We can't manage
when no one's applying for work.

630
00:51:49.857 --> 00:51:50.775
Not to mention,

631
00:51:52.777 --> 00:51:55.112
you and I are both…

632
00:51:56.864 --> 00:51:57.949
so exhausted.

633
00:52:06.082 --> 00:52:09.335
We managed so far,
however tough things were.

634
00:52:14.674 --> 00:52:16.133
I promised.

635
00:52:21.347 --> 00:52:23.850
I promised Dad
I'd keep the restaurant open.

636
00:52:33.109 --> 00:52:35.695
No. I can't keep doing this.

637
00:52:38.281 --> 00:52:40.575
I came this far, and that's good enough.

638
00:52:42.285 --> 00:52:43.536
I tried.

639
00:52:44.745 --> 00:52:46.163
They'll understand.

640
00:52:47.206 --> 00:52:48.082
Even Dad.

641
00:52:52.712 --> 00:52:53.754
Dad…

642
00:53:00.720 --> 00:53:02.847
This is exactly what they want.

643
00:53:03.431 --> 00:53:05.808
They want Famiglia to close and disappear.

644
00:53:07.059 --> 00:53:09.103
They want Dad to be erased.

645
00:53:12.356 --> 00:53:13.941
If I give up on Famiglia

646
00:53:15.985 --> 00:53:17.653
just because things are hard…

647
00:53:25.786 --> 00:53:26.746
Where are you going?

648
00:53:26.829 --> 00:53:30.374
I'll go and convince Mr. Park
to supply us just a few more days.

649
00:53:31.000 --> 00:53:33.711
And I'll try to persuade the section head

650
00:53:33.794 --> 00:53:35.421
to stay until the end of the month.

651
00:53:36.088 --> 00:53:38.007
I'll do whatever it takes
to get what we need,

652
00:53:38.090 --> 00:53:39.508
whether it's ingredients or staff.

653
00:53:59.195 --> 00:54:00.071
What's that noise?

654
00:54:06.285 --> 00:54:08.204
Is the cooling fan malfunctioning?

655
00:54:14.919 --> 00:54:15.962
I don't think it is.

656
00:54:18.130 --> 00:54:19.966
That's just odd.

657
00:56:07.782 --> 00:56:09.658
Cooking isn't about science or skill.

658
00:56:09.742 --> 00:56:10.868
It's about the heart.

659
00:56:25.132 --> 00:56:29.345
To cook for the one person
who will eat the food.

660
00:56:42.691 --> 00:56:45.611
To move that person with your sincerity.

661
00:57:04.213 --> 00:57:06.298
That's what real cuisine is.

662
00:57:06.382 --> 00:57:08.843
Just like the food you'll eat here today.

663
00:57:14.640 --> 00:57:16.058
Hey, Chef Choi. Over here.

664
00:57:23.607 --> 00:57:24.608
Man…

665
00:57:26.819 --> 00:57:27.903
This is my son, Han.

666
00:57:30.156 --> 00:57:31.574
Say hello, Han.

667
00:57:31.657 --> 00:57:33.659
He's the head chef of Famiglia.

668
00:58:00.728 --> 00:58:01.979
I'll have the signature course.

669
00:58:02.062 --> 00:58:03.814
Okay. Thank you.

670
00:58:15.451 --> 00:58:17.244
She didn't even ask which wine I'd like.

671
00:58:18.871 --> 00:58:21.290
It's early, but still,
no other customers?

672
00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:24.543
This is definitely the place
I visited long ago.

673
00:58:25.377 --> 00:58:27.213
Nothing has changed much.

674
00:58:29.381 --> 00:58:30.299
So what is

675
00:58:31.467 --> 00:58:33.219
this chilling sense I feel?

676
00:58:35.554 --> 00:58:37.932
The raw odor

677
00:58:39.475 --> 00:58:40.768
of freshly thawed frozen meat.

678
00:58:45.773 --> 00:58:47.191
What do you mean?

679
00:58:48.525 --> 00:58:49.985
Chef Choi Seung-hyo is dead?

680
00:58:50.069 --> 00:58:51.070
Well…

681
00:58:52.321 --> 00:58:54.240
It's quite unfortunate. I'm sorry.

682
00:58:56.909 --> 00:59:01.538
I hoped to taste Famiglia's food again
after ten years.

683
00:59:02.748 --> 00:59:04.500
Don't be too disappointed.

684
00:59:04.583 --> 00:59:07.336
To welcome you to Korea, Ms. Seon here

685
00:59:07.419 --> 00:59:09.838
reserved a table
at the best restaurant in Korea.

686
00:59:09.922 --> 00:59:11.757
You know Exception, don't you?

687
00:59:12.466 --> 00:59:14.510
Cha Woo-jin's Exception.

688
00:59:15.177 --> 00:59:18.472
We've asked Chef Cha
to prepare the food with extra care,

689
00:59:18.555 --> 00:59:21.558
so tonight's dinner will be
a special experience.

690
00:59:22.726 --> 00:59:23.894
Isn't that right, Ms. Seon?

691
00:59:25.271 --> 00:59:26.146
Yes.

692
00:59:28.691 --> 00:59:30.818
ANTIPASTO
SEARED SCALLOPS WITH VONGOLE SAUCE

693
01:00:04.435 --> 01:00:05.394
How is it?

694
01:00:06.895 --> 01:00:09.398
It's fresh scallops
seared quickly over high heat,

695
01:00:10.024 --> 01:00:12.109
served with a classic clam sauce.

696
01:00:12.985 --> 01:00:13.819
Delicious, right?

697
01:00:23.746 --> 01:00:26.415
SHRIMP RAVIOLI

698
01:00:37.009 --> 01:00:37.843
Is it good, son?

699
01:00:39.303 --> 01:00:41.388
It's the best. It's so good, Dad.

700
01:00:55.402 --> 01:00:56.362
It's gone bad.

701
01:01:05.746 --> 01:01:06.830
Oh dear.

702
01:01:08.374 --> 01:01:09.375
I apologize.

703
01:01:09.917 --> 01:01:11.835
This thing is pretty old.

704
01:01:20.511 --> 01:01:23.222
SPINACH RISOTTO

705
01:01:26.683 --> 01:01:28.852
When you scoop it up,

706
01:01:28.936 --> 01:01:30.938
it should gently flow
off the back of the spoon.

707
01:01:31.939 --> 01:01:34.650
That's the perfect risotto texture.

708
01:01:48.747 --> 01:01:50.082
The perfect risotto?

709
01:01:54.586 --> 01:01:57.714
MAIN DISH
BLACK GOAT SIRLOIN STEAK

710
01:02:02.678 --> 01:02:04.721
The delectable pink flesh.

711
01:02:05.764 --> 01:02:07.266
Don't you want a piece?

712
01:02:08.392 --> 01:02:10.936
Han, why won't you eat
this delicious food?

713
01:02:11.645 --> 01:02:13.730
This is what real cuisine is.

714
01:02:13.814 --> 01:02:16.984
Food that moves the diner's heart.

715
01:02:18.318 --> 01:02:20.320
Smelly scallops and spoiled ravioli.

716
01:02:21.697 --> 01:02:23.991
A perfectly sludgy risotto.

717
01:02:25.993 --> 01:02:28.287
And a main dish that's dry to the core.

718
01:02:28.871 --> 01:02:33.792
I want you to remember
this moment forever, Han.

719
01:02:36.795 --> 01:02:38.547
A moment to remember forever.

720
01:02:50.809 --> 01:02:52.269
Take me to Famiglia.

721
01:02:56.315 --> 01:02:58.942
What do you mean, Monsieur Bernier?

722
01:02:59.693 --> 01:03:01.862
Why go to a restaurant without a chef?

723
01:03:06.825 --> 01:03:07.701
Hello.

724
01:03:26.011 --> 01:03:27.554
For one last time,

725
01:03:27.638 --> 01:03:29.598
I wish to eat Famiglia's food

726
01:03:30.474 --> 01:03:32.643
and remember Chef Choi.

727
01:03:35.812 --> 01:03:36.855
It's a nightmare.

728
01:03:37.439 --> 01:03:38.524
Pardon?

729
01:03:38.607 --> 01:03:41.693
Cooking isn't just about
serving good food.

730
01:03:43.237 --> 01:03:45.697
Food can bring back
someone's precious memories.

731
01:03:46.615 --> 01:03:49.201
It can also give them courage to live on.

732
01:03:50.202 --> 01:03:51.370
What you served today

733
01:03:52.371 --> 01:03:54.498
turned a great memory I had for 26 years

734
01:03:55.582 --> 01:03:57.000
into a nightmare.

735
01:04:06.385 --> 01:04:08.303
What an unorganized kitchen.

736
01:04:11.723 --> 01:04:13.225
There's no regard for basic hygiene.

737
01:04:15.769 --> 01:04:18.272
And there's one chef
preparing the signature course alone.

738
01:04:20.190 --> 01:04:21.316
Who are you?

739
01:04:21.400 --> 01:04:22.317
The sous-chef?

740
01:04:22.401 --> 01:04:23.443
The
chef de partie?

741
01:04:25.404 --> 01:04:28.490
Where's the head chef,
and how dare they let you serve such food?

742
01:04:30.117 --> 01:04:33.161
The quality of the ingredients,
the seasoning,

743
01:04:33.245 --> 01:04:35.747
the viscosity of the sauce and purée,
and the overcooked meat!

744
01:04:38.584 --> 01:04:40.168
The whole thing was a disaster.

745
01:04:44.214 --> 01:04:45.841
How could this place go so far downhill?

746
01:04:48.093 --> 01:04:49.595
All that money and fame.

747
01:04:50.679 --> 01:04:51.930
Did it go to your head?

748
01:04:54.725 --> 01:04:56.393
You should be ashamed

749
01:04:57.060 --> 01:05:00.439
for disgracing Famiglia's name
by serving such trash!

750
01:05:01.940 --> 01:05:03.400
Watch what you say!

751
01:05:06.612 --> 01:05:08.697
My dad never, not even once,

752
01:05:10.198 --> 01:05:12.326
let anything get to his head.

753
01:05:15.037 --> 01:05:17.539
That's why he left a wronged man!

754
01:05:19.082 --> 01:05:20.083
What is she talking about?

755
01:05:21.126 --> 01:05:22.085
"Dad"?

756
01:05:32.971 --> 01:05:34.473
I don't care about that.

757
01:05:36.308 --> 01:05:37.893
I'm here as a customer.

758
01:05:37.976 --> 01:05:40.103
I came here to eat Famiglia's food.

759
01:05:40.687 --> 01:05:43.815
The kitchen may be a mess,
the ingredients might not be ready,

760
01:05:43.899 --> 01:05:45.567
and the service might be terrible!

761
01:05:46.318 --> 01:05:49.529
Even if the head chef
left the restaurant to be on TV,

762
01:05:50.906 --> 01:05:54.993
you should've served
Famiglia's signature dishes to perfection.

763
01:05:56.787 --> 01:05:59.081
This dismal place can't be Famiglia!

764
01:06:04.711 --> 01:06:07.172
-Song-yi. Are you okay?
-Auntie.

765
01:06:11.343 --> 01:06:12.177
Auntie.

766
01:06:29.986 --> 01:06:31.279
Dad…

767
01:06:36.410 --> 01:06:37.828
Dad…

768
01:07:12.904 --> 01:07:13.739
Get down.

769
01:07:18.285 --> 01:07:19.119
I said get down.

770
01:07:19.202 --> 01:07:20.162
What?

771
01:07:25.917 --> 01:07:26.918
Get down!

772
01:08:48.208 --> 01:08:49.626
By the way,

773
01:08:49.709 --> 01:08:51.670
what is it that you do?

774
01:08:52.462 --> 01:08:53.547
It's been ten years.

775
01:08:53.630 --> 01:08:54.798
Henri Bernier?

776
01:08:54.881 --> 01:08:56.591
I'd like you to serve dinner tonight.

777
01:08:59.553 --> 01:09:01.096
-Go.
-What is this?

778
01:09:01.179 --> 01:09:02.430
It's perfect.

779
01:09:02.514 --> 01:09:03.974
Find out quickly who he is.

780
01:09:04.641 --> 01:09:06.935
What is his connection to Famiglia?

781
01:09:07.018 --> 01:09:08.478
The best K-chef?

782
01:09:10.605 --> 01:09:11.565
That man from yesterday.

783
01:09:11.648 --> 01:09:14.025
I'm offering you a deal, Ms. Choi.

784
01:09:14.109 --> 01:09:16.403
I want to show them for once

785
01:09:16.486 --> 01:09:19.698
-Dad!
-that they can't always have their way.

786
01:09:19.781 --> 01:09:20.949
Help me.

787
01:09:27.289 --> 01:09:30.292
Subtitle: Jennifer Jean Lim

